From 6b02c6d071dc7efc9700a22ad25d3da352f2b51c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment <experiment@invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:38:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: do not treat the cyclic data PID as a re-arm
 wrap

The fifth lifecycle boot completed its first lifetime, both key
removals and the deferred re-arm request, and the re-arm pass then
refused with "rearm wrap: next_pid=82" and poisoned the lifetime. The
join PID counter is synced from the data PID pool, which cycles through
its range during every data phase and restarts with the epoch; its
value at the terminal is wherever the last data frame left it. The
previous two boots passed this clause by luck (PIDs 10 and 15). Drop
the clause: the wrap rule keeps the channel token, the station
sequence and the command sequence, which are the boot-scoped
identities it was written for.

Internal experiment archive; synthetic non-certifying author,
not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-rearm.h | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-rearm.h b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-rearm.h
index e3c9493b4..d0e1445fd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-rearm.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-rearm.h
@@ -43,8 +43,11 @@ mt6797_join_rearm_ready(const struct mt6797_join_rearm_state *s)
 	    s->inflight || s->page_debt || s->data_page_debt || s->credit_pending ||
 	    !s->queue_empty)
 		return MT6797_JOIN_REARM_NO;
-	if (s->channel_token == 255 || s->sta_sequence == 255 || s->sequence > 248 ||
-	    s->next_pid > 63)
+	/* The data PID is cyclic and the pool restarts with the epoch, so it
+	 * is not a boot-scoped identity: the fifth lifecycle boot stopped its
+	 * data phase at PID 82 and was refused here as a wrap.
+	 */
+	if (s->channel_token == 255 || s->sta_sequence == 255 || s->sequence > 248)
 		return MT6797_JOIN_REARM_WRAP;
 	return MT6797_JOIN_REARM_YES;
 }
